{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact 70e6887ca2b04e8c24160915a0e313a834eb6d70 for row-write accounting request git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8bd623cc41cf18c9189bb6e716b56431edc18d10 (#8900), resolving the composition requirement in review git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4691585535af5d330c6905005c1daa99dac8aa70 (#10562). All 39 artifacts were individually inspected as effective, at this head, directly on builder promise git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f3d305c3d4defed39ac3e9c9b8f7326e239fba7 (#8901); packages/room/measure/README.md is primary.\n\nThe recut keeps main 965c911a's complete job-token scheduling block: jobTokensDue, the canonical-repository-gone fence and that loop kind's own backoff. Check jobs retain jobsDue, the mint ledger retains its due time and fence, and the safe-error scrub keeps its independent wake. The delayed-pin path contributes its due time once and passes it to loopPendingKinds. The default path keeps the bounded-result existence query. The earliest eligible candidate wins. I read merge 3894d60e's resolution, its new composed test, the main-relative production delta and the report changes. Both new commits carry the full request trailer. A separate git merge-tree against current main d3f7d3a8b2b8cc44c7a6bf3c0d5eb942dc18057c is clean.\n\nArchitecture: ordinary Git implementation (Gitseq layer 1), coordinated through Workroom and projections (5-7); no kernel, nexus or host-binding contract changes. Within Artroom, one scheduler composes existing owners' due times without taking over their responsibilities. The existing pin/publication/ownership contracts and the operator-approved default-off measurement switch remain intact. The earlier main conflict is resolved, with no second scheduler or new lifecycle.\n\nSecurity: no unresolved defect found in this change. Re-inspected effective implementation request #8900, builder promise #8901 and the operator's spike-only authorization git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:66a41558f53c0e1baf5abdcb6cec8074b5bc3a29 (#9651). The switch remains off by default; this verdict grants no production setting or provider action. Mutation controls prove the composed pin, mint and job-token fences and backoffs remain effective. Inherited mint-C implementation and authority adoption were independently reviewed in git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:132f4eec1f65fb8bfe8fe1ed79cf7734a0b7d9d4 (#10444), landed by receipt git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72bf6ea32c2b1017963d3dc0eca55f9de823eb1e (#10452); this recut preserves that implementation. The authority-bearing chain's four facts were confirmed in that review, not newly inferred from this merge.\n\nSimplification: the earlier improvement stands: one SELECT 1 ... LIMIT 1 check when pin delay is off, one SQL aggregate over due keys when on, and the aggregate passed through rather than recomputed. No additional abstraction is needed. The new composition test exercises all five candidates in one room while the earlier focused tests preserve each mechanism's own checks. The normal-path one-row result is for the tested pending backlog, not a promise about every possible completed-pin history. The measurement-only aggregate remains proportional to the due rows.\n\nEvidence at this head:\n- Fresh npm ci in both disposable clones. Root npm test exit 0: 2,372 passed, one skipped; root typecheck exit 0.\n- Git Workers tests: 11 passed. Room-local Wrangler 4.146 dry-run bundle exit 0, no upload.\n- Twenty-two independent scheduler mutations all loaded and caused named runtime test failures. The 18 controls from revision 4 were rerun, plus removal of the check-job candidate, removal of the token-revocation candidate, removal of its gone-repository fence, and removal of its own backoff. Each of those four fails the new composed-with-lane-C test. No compilation, transform or startup failure is counted as a guard result.\n- After restoration, 81 focused tests passed: 16 pin/composition tests, the two unchanged independent backlog controls, nine safe-error tests, 21 founding tests and 33 mint-sites tests. The original 5,000-pending-pin control still reads one row; the 150,000-row control still completes. The two committed pin-backlog tests also passed in the full root suite.\n- All mutations restored and the temporary checker test removed; both clones clean at the exact head; git diff --check clean. Logs and mutation scripts/results are under /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v5*.\n- The accounting gate, smoke driver, scheduled workflow, budgets and their row/check/budget tests are byte-identical to revision 4. The 29 earlier accounting mutations and the provider-sample reconstruction in review git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8698e20fbe8396dbe78b8122f3a8912952d99904 (#10290) are carried evidence, not claimed as rerun here. The full suite does rerun their committed tests.\n\nMeasurement and operational limits: the report now explicitly identifies e50e062a as the measured Room code, before mint lanes B and C. The saved provider samples and earlier raw-versus-adjusted qualifications remain the evidence; this review does not treat those costs as measurements of 70e6887c. Pinning, proposing, landing, publication, policy activation and smoke totals must be measured again after a deployment, and the ceilings grounded again. The existing fail-closed gate is retained; this approval does not waive it or assert that the scheduled workflow's operator-supplied secret/enable flag is configured. Budget enforcement remains with its separate request, as the report says. Time-relative historical wording such as lane C not yet being on main is superseded by this exact-head account and should be dated when the measurement report is refreshed.\n\nThe already tracked live propose 503 investigation git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:df6ff8d361dc8940e66f9eb59d8cad91d001ffca (#10572) remains separate and open. Passing local controls here establishes neither a diagnosis nor a healthy live spike. Its builder-reserved environment was untouched: no live provider queries, credentials, deployment or canonical checkout edits occurred. This verdict closes the row-writes review, not that incident or the fresh-measurement obligation.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b600a27a616a83ec84f91b8d4b1673e165c510f1","binding":"assigned","head":"70e6887ca2b04e8c24160915a0e313a834eb6d70","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ccce390e586bed6d86d107fb20f357c57d92f0f7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f3d305c3d4defed39ac3e9c9b8f7326e239fba7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:079151998d1e28c98611e300a1240add8dcc04b5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}